# Subtitles are one sentence

Every subtitle on the docs site — the `description` on `DocPage`, and the
description on any grouped section — is a single sentence. Say what the thing
is, as briefly as it can be said, and stop.

Do not append a second sentence of usage guidance ("Use X when…", "Prefer Y
over Z…"). That is documentation, and this site shows components rather than
explaining them. If two facts genuinely both matter, merge them into one
sentence instead of adding another.

```tsx
// Yes
description="Single-choice menu for forms and filters."

// No — the second sentence is guidance
description="Single-choice menu for forms and filters. Prefer select when options are longer than a short radio group."
```
